data the previous one created, so the sequence matters:

@06_member1_onboarding.sql          Member 1
@07_member2_skills.sql              Member 2
@08_member3_booking.sql             Member 3
@09_member4_credit.sql              Member 4
@10_member5_feedback_disputes.sql   Member 5
@11_group_tcl_plans.sql             everyone, together

Each member file holds exactly 9 queries: 1 INSERT, 1 UPDATE,
1 DELETE and 6 SELECTs (simple, join, nested, correlated,
aggregate, analytic). See QUERY_PLAN.md for the full breakdown.

